  "question": {
    "text": "If <math><msub><mrow><mi>z</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>z</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math>&nbsp;are two distinct complex numbers satisfying the relation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>-</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><msub><mover><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><msub><mover><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mover><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mover><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> and&nbsp;<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">arg</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>z</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>-</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">arg</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>z</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>, then the least possible value of <math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is equal to (where,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi></math>&nbsp;are integers)"
  },
